In a certain year, an economy has the following data:

- real GDP in the first year: 18 400 billion FCFA; in the second year: 19 504 billion FCFA;
- labour force: 9.5 million people, of whom 760 000 are unemployed;
- population growth over the year: 3.5%.

(a) Calculate the rate of economic growth and the rate of unemployment.

(b) Explain, with a calculation, why the growth may not improve the average standard of living much.
